=B. The station suggests both loss and connection because its abandoned windows show closure while the worn benches support the source's idea that transit spaces hold traces of shared movement.#Correct. This uses both sources to support analysis. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~C. Transit spaces are symbols, so the station must be the most important setting in the story.#This overstates the source and adds an unsupported claim. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~D. The benches are smooth because people sat on them.#This explains the literal detail without analyzing it. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}
